---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Ornament from '../components/Ornament.astro';
import { SOURCES } from '../lib/data';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology, Sources & Testing"
  description="How AlbionForge computes profit: the formulas, game constants with sources and dates, hand-computed test scenarios, and our AI-use disclosure."
  canonical="/methodology/"
  keywords={['albionforge methodology', 'albion calculator sources', 'albion return rate formula']}
>
  <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Methodology</div>
  <article class="section prose">
    <h1>Methodology, Sources &amp; Testing</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Trustworthy arithmetic needs visible working. This page shows every formula, every game
      constant with its source, and how the math is tested.
    </p>

    <h2>The formulas</h2>
    <p>All four calculators run on one small, pure engine:</p>
    <div class="formula">
      return&nbsp;rate&nbsp;=&nbsp;production&nbsp;bonus&nbsp;÷&nbsp;(100&nbsp;+&nbsp;production&nbsp;bonus)<br />
      net&nbsp;material&nbsp;cost&nbsp;=&nbsp;Σ(qty&nbsp;×&nbsp;price)&nbsp;×&nbsp;(1&nbsp;−&nbsp;return&nbsp;rate)&nbsp;·&nbsp;per&nbsp;returnable&nbsp;line<br />
      sale&nbsp;proceeds&nbsp;=&nbsp;price&nbsp;×&nbsp;qty&nbsp;×&nbsp;(1&nbsp;−&nbsp;sales&nbsp;tax&nbsp;[−&nbsp;setup&nbsp;fee&nbsp;if&nbsp;order])<br />
      profit&nbsp;=&nbsp;proceeds&nbsp;+&nbsp;returns&nbsp;sold&nbsp;−&nbsp;net&nbsp;material&nbsp;cost&nbsp;−&nbsp;fees<br />
      profit&nbsp;per&nbsp;focus&nbsp;=&nbsp;profit&nbsp;÷&nbsp;(focus&nbsp;per&nbsp;craft&nbsp;×&nbsp;crafts)<br />
      break-even&nbsp;sell&nbsp;=&nbsp;invested&nbsp;÷&nbsp;(qty&nbsp;×&nbsp;(1&nbsp;−&nbsp;tax&nbsp;fraction))
    </div>
    <p>
      “Reuse returns” (the default) nets returned materials against the next craft - the standard
      community model. “Sell returns” values them at your entered prices minus the sales tax. Both
      are labelled in each calculator's assumptions line.
    </p>

    <h2>Game constants and their sources</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="ledger">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Fact</th><th>Value used</th><th>Source</th><th>Verified</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Return-rate formula &amp; bonus points</td>
            <td>bonus ÷ (100+bonus); city +18, refining city +40, crafting city +15, focus +59</td>
            <td><a href={SOURCES.rrr} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Albion Free Market</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>City refining specialisations</td>
            <td>Thetford bars · FS planks · Martlock leather · Lymhurst cloth · Bridgewatch blocks</td>
            <td><a href={SOURCES.wikiRefiningArchive} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official wiki (archived)</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Refining recipes &amp; base focus</td>
            <td>T2–T8: 1–5 raw + 1 lower; focus 18/31/54/94/164/287/503</td>
            <td><a href={SOURCES.recipes} rel="noopener" target="_blank">AOScout</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Market tax structure</td>
            <td>2.5% setup fee (orders, non-refundable) · 4% sales tax · 2% with Premium</td>
            <td><a href={SOURCES.taxWorked} rel="noopener" target="_blank">AFM worked examples</a> · <a href={SOURCES.wikiMarketArchive} rel="noopener" target="_blank">wiki (archived)</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Focus cost formula</td>
            <td>base × 0.5^(efficiency ÷ 10,000)</td>
            <td><a href={SOURCES.focusSpec} rel="noopener" target="_blank">AFM focus analysis</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Station fee formula</td>
            <td>nutrition = item value × 0.1125 · fee = nutrition × rate ÷ 100</td>
            <td><a href={SOURCES.stationFees} rel="noopener" target="_blank">AFM station fees</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Enchant components</td>
            <td>.1 runes · .2 souls · .3 relics · .4 Avalonian shards (counts vary by slot)</td>
            <td><a href="https://albiononline.com/news/guide-crafting" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official crafting guide</a> · <a href={SOURCES.taxWorked} rel="noopener" target="_blank">AFM melding</a></td>
            <td>2026-10</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">
      Sandbox Interactive changes numbers in patches. Every preset is editable in the calculators,
      and we re-verify the table above after major economy patches - see the
      <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Testing</h2>
    <p>
      The engine is a pure TypeScript module with no browser dependencies, covered by Vitest
      scenarios whose expected values are <strong>hand-computed with plain arithmetic</strong> (the
      same numbers printed in the worked examples on each tool page). The suite checks:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Refining: 100× T5 bars in a bonus city (36.7% return) → net cost 160,782, profit +242,418, break-even 1,674.81.</li>
      <li>Crafting: artifact jacket batch → net materials 118,198.68/craft, profit +53,401.32/craft, break-even 124,373.63.</li>
      <li>Transport: 500 bars Martlock→Thetford → 8 trips, profit +354,000, break-even sell 4,062.5.</li>
      <li>Enchanting: .0→.1 upgrade → profit +79,720.25, premium over selling base +83,320.25.</li>
      <li>Tax edge cases: instant sell vs sell order, Premium halving, buy-order setup fee.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small">Run them yourself: <span class="mono">npm test</span> in the repository.</p>

    <h2>AI-use disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      AlbionForge's pages and code were drafted with AI assistance and are reviewed, corrected and
      owned by the site maintainer. Every game number was independently checked against the cited
      sources at publishing time; two of our own initial guesses (the crafting city bonus and two
      city specialisations) were wrong and fixed during that verification - which is exactly why
      this page exists.
    </p>

    <h2>Measurement &amp; privacy</h2>
    <p>
      We run no analytics - no GA4, no counters, no cookies. The trade-off is deliberate: we
      measure success by the only signal that matters for a static tool, whether visitors finish
      their calculation and come back, and we keep the promise that nothing you type leaves your
      browser. Hosting logs (Cloudflare Pages) exist solely to serve the site.
    </p>

    <Ornament />
    <p>
      Spotted an error? <a href="/about/">Contact us</a> - corrections are credited in the
      <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
